WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:15.416
[insects chittering]

2
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.500
[rumbling]

3
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.250
[rumbling intensifies]

4
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:42.875
[train whistle blows in distance]

5
00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:44.916
[rumbling]

6
00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:52.458
[dishes rattling]

7
00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:56.166
[train rattling in distance]

8
00:00:56.833 --> 00:00:59.416
It's coming! It's coming!
It's coming! Come on!

9
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.708
[man 1] The earth is shaking!

10
00:01:00.791 --> 00:01:03.375
[panting] It's here!

11
00:01:03.458 --> 00:01:04.541
[woman] What's here?

12
00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:06.958
- [man 2] Calm down!
- The ground is moving!

13
00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:09.000
- What's coming? What is it?
- A beast.

14
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:11.041
Like a beast that's pulling a town.

15
00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:13.000
- [train whistle blows in distance]
- [rumbling]

16
00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:14.000
It's here.

17
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.750
[dogs barking in distance]

18
00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.166
[train whistle blows in distance]

19
00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.291
Hey. kid. come on.
Come on. You're gonna miss it.

20
00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:26.625
Mama Úrsula.

21
00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:28.375
[chuckles] It's here.

22
00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:29.291
What is here?

23
00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:32.208
[clavichord music playing]

24
00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.500
[man] Hurry up. run!

25
00:01:35.625 --> 00:01:37.708
[woman] It's here! It's here!

26
00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:40.958
- Meme. leave that. Come on.
- [Fernanda] Where are you going?

27
00:01:41.041 --> 00:01:42.166
It's almost here.

28
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.166
May we go. Mama?

29
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.666
You may. after your lesson. Renata.

30
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.791
Fernanda. let her go.

31
00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:50.500
Can I go. Mama?

32
00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:55.291
Let's go. let's go. let's go.

33
00:01:57.125 --> 00:02:00.083
- [young José Arcadio] Careful. Meme. Wait.
- Come on. come on. come on.

34
00:02:00.166 --> 00:02:02.791
Grab my arm. Grab my arm!
Less talking. more moving.

35
00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:04.583
- Grab my arm.
- [Úrsula] For goodness' sake. Careful.

36
00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:07.333
- [Aureliano II] Forget the shawl.
- [Úrsula] Don't take off your shawl.

37
00:02:07.416 --> 00:02:09.041
- [door slams]
- [Úrsula] Remedios!

38
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:12.458
Remedios! Put this on.

39
00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:14.541
[train whistle blowing in distance]

40
00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:22.583
[woman] Come on. children. Come quick!

41
00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:25.166
[narrator] <i>The innocent train</i>
<i>that would bring to Macondo</i>

42
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.083
<i>so many uncertainties and truths.</i>

43
00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:30.500
<i>so much praise and misfortune.</i>

44
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:35.583
<i>and so many changes. calamities.</i>
<i>and longings had finally arrived.</i>

45
00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:37.666
[train rattling]

46
00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:44.791
[Aureliano II] Welcome to Macondo!

47
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:46.041
[exclaims excitedly]

48
00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:49.416
[narrator] <i>The people of Macondo watched</i>
<i>as José Arcadio Segundo</i>

49
00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.625
<i>and Aureliano Triste</i>
<i>waved from the top of the locomotive.</i>

50
00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:56.458
[screams joyfully]

51
00:02:57.541 --> 00:02:59.791
- You're here. brother! You're here!
- Isn't this amazing?

52
00:02:59.875 --> 00:03:00.791
- Uncle!
- Where is he?

53
00:03:01.541 --> 00:03:04.000
[man 1] It's here! We did it. Macondo!

54
00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.458
[man 2] Welcome to Macondo!

55
00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:07.541
[dramatic music playing]

56
00:03:09.958 --> 00:03:13.416
Your great-grandfather
would be so proud. José Arcadio.

57
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:17.166
You made his lifelong dream come true.

58
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.625
You connected Macondo with the world.

59
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:22.333
Well done. son.

60
00:03:25.291 --> 00:03:28.208
Now. you really have proven
half of the town wrong. brother.

61
00:03:28.291 --> 00:03:29.833
It was worth the wait. wasn't it?

62
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.458
- Come on. Where are we going?
- To the train.

63
00:03:33.541 --> 00:03:35.250
No. Meme.

64
00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:37.166
- Come on. Let's go on the train.
- Stop. no. No.

65
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.250
- Mom is going to get angry.
- So what? Don't be dumb.

66
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:42.125
No. Meme. Where are we going?

67
00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:44.083
[man 1] Welcome to Macondo. Welcome.

68
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:45.250
[woman] Hello.

69
00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:48.375
[man 2] I'm sorry. I've just arrived…

70
00:03:51.416 --> 00:03:52.416
Nothing to worry about!

71
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.125
Nothing to worry about.
ladies and gentlemen! That's right!

72
00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:57.291
Come on closer. Don't be afraid.

73
00:03:58.041 --> 00:04:00.541
[narrator] <i>A stranger</i>
<i>stepped off the train</i>

74
00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:04.083
<i>so elegant and dignified</i>

75
00:04:04.166 --> 00:04:09.041
<i>that Pietro Crespi himself</i>
<i>would have looked like a fop beside him.</i>

76
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:11.125
[dramatic music continues]

77
00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:22.166
Ah. pardon me.

78
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:25.625
Uh. mind telling me
where I could find a good restaurant?

79
00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:28.791
A new restaurant
that has authentic and traditional food.

80
00:04:29.791 --> 00:04:31.625
I know just the place. Mr…

81
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:33.166
Herbert.

82
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.458
Mr. Herbert. I would like to invite you
over for lunch at my house.

83
00:04:36.541 --> 00:04:38.750
where the finest food in all of Macondo
is prepared.

84
00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:40.750
- Isn't that right. Mama Úrsula?
- That's right.

85
00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:44.125
The Buendía house opens its doors
for this special occasion.

86
00:04:44.208 --> 00:04:46.541
- How wonderful.
- [Úrsula] Everyone is welcome.

87
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:49.375
- Our doors are open.
- [Mr. Herbert] Thank you so much.

88
00:04:49.458 --> 00:04:51.333
[conductor] Next stop. Fundación!

89
00:04:51.416 --> 00:04:53.125
[indistinct chattering]

90
00:04:57.041 --> 00:04:59.458
I found these two sitting
in the back of the train.

91
00:04:59.958 --> 00:05:02.250
Thank you so much. Miss. uh…

92
00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:03.750
Cotes.

93
00:05:04.375 --> 00:05:05.500
Cotes.

94
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.041
[Petra] Mm.

95
00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.625
Dad. who's that woman?
Why does she know us?

96
00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:15.750
Son. everybody here knows us.

97
00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:17.208
We are Buendías.

98
00:05:17.291 --> 00:05:18.916
- [Amaranta] José Arcadio.
- You…

99
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.041
- You disappeared. Where'd you go?
- Why'd you run off?

100
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:23.916
[young José Arcadio] It was Meme.
She dragged me onto the train. I swear.

101
00:05:24.541 --> 00:05:27.458
Welcome. Welcome to the Buendía household.

102
00:05:27.541 --> 00:05:30.375
Santa Sofía. go get two hens
from the back. please.

103
00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:32.583
We have to cook a bit of everything.

104
00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:34.791
You never know what foreigners
are going to want to eat.

105
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:37.291
[Mr. Herbert] Wow.
This place is like a dream.

106
00:05:37.375 --> 00:05:39.375
[clavichord music playing]

107
00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:44.125
[woman] Right over there.

108
00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:50.083
[José Arcadio II] Rum.
Welcome. Welcome to our home.

109
00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:53.375
Have some rum.

110
00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:57.625
Welcome to the Buendía household.

111
00:05:58.541 --> 00:05:59.500
[man] Thank you.

112
00:06:00.208 --> 00:06:01.333
[Fernanda] Aureliano?

113
00:06:01.875 --> 00:06:02.875
[man coughs]

114
00:06:04.041 --> 00:06:05.166
Aureliano?

115
00:06:06.916 --> 00:06:10.833
- [woman 2] Oh. she's playing great. Wow!
- Renata! Go to your room right now.

116
00:06:10.916 --> 00:06:13.291
- [woman 2] Why is she stopping?
- Aureliano?

117
00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:15.500
[woman 3] Do you think
there's sleeping beds here?

118
00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:18.083
[Fernanda] José Arcadio!

119
00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:23.041
[scoffs] Of course it was you
who brought this circus into the house.

120
00:06:24.208 --> 00:06:25.833
This circus is the future.

121
00:06:26.458 --> 00:06:29.291
And this is just the beginning.
so you might wanna get used to it.

122
00:06:30.541 --> 00:06:32.125
'Cause I am not my brother.

123
00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:35.500
[woman 4] Mrs. Buendía. how many people
are you having over for lunch?

124
00:06:35.583 --> 00:06:36.625
[José Arcadio II] Welcome.

125
00:06:38.208 --> 00:06:40.291
[Úrsula] We'll need the other set
for this many people.

126
00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:42.708
José Arcadio. leave that. Come.

127
00:06:43.791 --> 00:06:45.083
[Úrsula] That one. Bring me that.

128
00:06:45.166 --> 00:06:47.250
[Amaranta] Tell your mother
her reign is over.

129
00:06:47.333 --> 00:06:49.583
The Buendía house is chaotic once again.

130
00:06:50.125 --> 00:06:53.291
Mama. my aunt says
your reign is over and that--

131
00:06:53.375 --> 00:06:54.416
José Arcadio.

132
00:06:55.458 --> 00:06:57.208
- Go to your mom.
- [Fernanda] Aureliano.

133
00:06:57.291 --> 00:06:59.833
[intriguing music playing]

134
00:07:02.666 --> 00:07:05.333
- [all gasp]
- Oh. it startled me.

135
00:07:05.416 --> 00:07:08.208
[laughter]

136
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.625
Take me as your husband. I beg you.

137
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.500
[chuckles] That's a crazy thing to say.

138
00:07:23.583 --> 00:07:26.500
I promise you
that I will spend my entire life

139
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.375
doing everything in my power
to give the world to you.

140
00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:33.875
How will you do that?
You don't know anything about me. do you?

141
00:07:35.875 --> 00:07:37.125
Remedios.

142
00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:39.583
Go to the kitchen.

143
00:07:43.416 --> 00:07:45.208
Aren't you going to eat something?

144
00:07:45.708 --> 00:07:47.166
It's going to get cold.

145
00:07:49.041 --> 00:07:50.416
Well. gentlemen.

146
00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.125
the bell rings only once for supper
and once for Mass.

147
00:07:53.208 --> 00:07:54.500
- Thank you.
- Thank you. ma'am.

148
00:07:54.583 --> 00:07:57.666
[José Arcadio II] Please enjoy. everybody.
It's delicious. You're gonna love it.

149
00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.500
[indistinct chattering]

150
00:08:02.916 --> 00:08:04.416
[José Arcadio II] Enjoy. everybody.

151
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.416
[Mr. Herbert] Wow. this is really good.

152
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.250
[woman] José Arcadio.
bring some more juice.

153
00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:09.333
[man 2] Delicious.

154
00:08:09.416 --> 00:08:10.500
[woman 2] Chicken?

155
00:08:10.583 --> 00:08:13.166
[José Arcadio II] <i>Poulet?</i>
Oh. pass her the chicken. please.

156
00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.708
[man 3 belches. groans]

157
00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:23.208
[Mr. Herbert] Oh!

158
00:08:24.291 --> 00:08:25.375
What is this?

159
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.833
Banana.

160
00:08:27.541 --> 00:08:28.833
- You eat it.
- You eat it?

161
00:08:28.916 --> 00:08:29.833
Mm-hmm.

162
00:08:34.708 --> 00:08:35.958
Banana. anyone?

163
00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:49.666
[bird chirping]

164
00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.750
[dramatic music playing]

165
00:09:19.208 --> 00:09:24.625
ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE

166
00:09:25.291 --> 00:09:27.375
[José Arcadio II]
You can find these things everywhere.

167
00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:29.416
and they grow very quickly.

168
00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.791
[Mr. Herbert] Remarkable.

169
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.875
Uh. um. do you know where there's more?

170
00:09:34.958 --> 00:09:37.625
Oh. I'm happy to take you
all over the outskirts of Macondo.

171
00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:39.000
It's full of bananas.

172
00:09:39.708 --> 00:09:41.166
Much appreciated. young man.

173
00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.500
Yeah. my pleasure.

174
00:09:42.583 --> 00:09:44.833
[Aureliano] Who brought these gringos
into this house?

175
00:09:44.916 --> 00:09:46.791
[guests murmuring]

176
00:09:46.875 --> 00:09:49.541
- Get out of here!
- [José Arcadio II] Hey. settle down. sir.

177
00:09:50.916 --> 00:09:52.625
The thing is

178
00:09:52.708 --> 00:09:56.041
that all of these nice travelers here
are Great-Grandmother's guests.

179
00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:58.375
Go talk to her.

180
00:09:58.458 --> 00:10:01.041
This is the last thing
I need to see in Macondo.

181
00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.708
Our house getting invaded
by the same sons of bitches

182
00:10:05.791 --> 00:10:07.666
that stole Panama from us.

183
00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.666
[woman] What does he mean "Panama"?

184
00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.000
[Aureliano] Bastards.

185
00:10:11.875 --> 00:10:15.083
- Úrsula!
- Please excuse the old man. He's. uh…

186
00:10:15.166 --> 00:10:16.583
Well. he's lost his mind.

187
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.750
He couldn't kill himself
and leave us in peace!

188
00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:23.083
Uh…

189
00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:26.458
No. it's really no problem at all.

190
00:10:26.541 --> 00:10:28.333
I'm loving Macondo.

191
00:10:28.416 --> 00:10:31.166
Everyone is. uh. very passionate.

192
00:10:32.958 --> 00:10:33.958
It's very pretty.

193
00:10:34.041 --> 00:10:36.250
I told you. They grow everywhere.

194
00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.583
- Oh my goodness.
- [intriguing music playing]

195
00:10:39.083 --> 00:10:41.625
Oh my goodness. Would you look…

196
00:10:42.333 --> 00:10:43.791
So many.

197
00:10:46.666 --> 00:10:48.166
Who owns all of it?

198
00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.666
Oh. it's everyone's.

199
00:10:50.166 --> 00:10:52.000
- All of it?
- Mm-hmm. The people's.

200
00:10:52.083 --> 00:10:54.083
[train whistle blowing]

201
00:10:58.583 --> 00:11:01.666
[narrator] <i>The arrival of the train</i>
<i>unleashed a wave of excitement</i>

202
00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:02.958
<i>no one could contain.</i>

203
00:11:03.041 --> 00:11:05.041
[music intensifies]

204
00:11:14.125 --> 00:11:15.625
- [Fernanda] Renata!
- [gasps]

205
00:11:15.708 --> 00:11:17.750
You are not to be outside
when those people are here.

206
00:11:17.833 --> 00:11:20.083
- Go to your room!
- [Sofía] Everybody. this way. please.

207
00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.291
We call that <i>"papoche."</i>

208
00:11:23.375 --> 00:11:24.916
We throw those to the animals.

209
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.708
This one is delicious.

210
00:11:26.791 --> 00:11:28.291
Incredibly sweet. hmm?

211
00:11:28.375 --> 00:11:31.166
[narrator] <i>The people of Macondo</i>
<i>surrendered to the endless bounty</i>

212
00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.750
<i>that came in the train cars…</i>

213
00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:34.250
[conductor] How are you doing?

214
00:11:34.333 --> 00:11:36.125
We can barely keep up.

215
00:11:36.208 --> 00:11:37.958
Look at what I brought for the kids.

216
00:11:38.041 --> 00:11:40.166
<i>…while foreigners found themselves</i>
<i>in a land</i>

217
00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:42.916
<i>where everything seemed to flourish</i>
<i>without measure.</i>

218
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.750
[lively music playing]

219
00:11:49.333 --> 00:11:51.208
Hide all of it. son.

220
00:11:53.458 --> 00:11:55.958
Fernanda has the kids
locked in their room.

221
00:12:00.333 --> 00:12:01.625
It's beautiful. sure.

222
00:12:02.208 --> 00:12:03.833
- Yeah.
- But it's a plague.

223
00:12:08.333 --> 00:12:09.916
[Mr. Herbert] Mm-hmm. Okay.

224
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
[lively music continues]

225
00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.583
It's beautiful.

226
00:12:23.666 --> 00:12:24.875
Paradise.

227
00:12:24.958 --> 00:12:25.916
Paradise.

228
00:12:32.291 --> 00:12:33.541
[music stops]

229
00:12:36.625 --> 00:12:37.666
[José Arcadio II] Colonel!

230
00:12:40.458 --> 00:12:41.500
[Aureliano] Mmm.

231
00:12:42.333 --> 00:12:44.333
Did you know that aside from the food.

232
00:12:44.916 --> 00:12:48.166
foreigners come to this house
to meet the family's madman?

233
00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.000
You're a real tourist attraction.

234
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.041
You think everything
that's happening in Macondo

235
00:12:54.125 --> 00:12:56.750
is just fine and wonderful. José Arcadio.

236
00:12:58.583 --> 00:13:00.541
because you're too stupid to see it.

237
00:13:01.333 --> 00:13:03.166
You don't understand
who the gringos really are.

238
00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:06.416
You have to change your tune
because the gringos are here to stay.

239
00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:10.333
Mr. Herbert told me
some merchants were coming from Ohio.

240
00:13:10.416 --> 00:13:13.583
and that they're buying
every single vacant lot around Macondo.

241
00:13:17.208 --> 00:13:20.083
Well. they'll find out
who really owns those lots.

242
00:13:20.833 --> 00:13:21.666
Imbecile.

243
00:13:24.958 --> 00:13:26.250
You old bastard.

244
00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:58.750
[insects chittering]

245
00:14:18.833 --> 00:14:20.833
[door hinge creaking]

246
00:14:27.958 --> 00:14:29.958
[dark music playing]

247
00:14:41.791 --> 00:14:43.208
[in Wayuu] What do you want?

248
00:14:44.166 --> 00:14:45.375
Get out of here.

249
00:14:53.583 --> 00:14:54.875
[in English] Rebeca.

250
00:14:55.375 --> 00:14:59.125
[narrator] <i>The colonel</i>
<i>immediately recognized his sister Rebeca.</i>

251
00:15:00.375 --> 00:15:03.625
<i>the one with the impatient heart</i>
<i>and the boundless womb.</i>

252
00:15:04.541 --> 00:15:06.458
<i>The only one with the unbridled courage</i>

253
00:15:06.541 --> 00:15:09.458
<i>Úrsula had always wished</i>
<i>to see in her bloodline.</i>

254
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.375
[Aureliano] I thought you were dead.
If we had known you were--

255
00:15:13.458 --> 00:15:17.250
Aureliano… I don't give a shit
about what happens

256
00:15:17.333 --> 00:15:19.166
beyond the walls of this house.

257
00:15:19.916 --> 00:15:22.875
And what happens to the Buendías
matters even less.

258
00:15:24.625 --> 00:15:27.583
To me. it's as if
the family died with José Arcadio.

259
00:15:48.208 --> 00:15:50.541
Tell me once and for all
why you've come here.

260
00:15:51.458 --> 00:15:53.250
or I'll shoot your head off.

261
00:16:00.833 --> 00:16:03.208
The land that surrounds Macondo.

262
00:16:08.125 --> 00:16:11.458
I know Arcadio gave those property titles
to my brother.

263
00:16:14.208 --> 00:16:16.583
And if those lands have rightful owners.

264
00:16:17.583 --> 00:16:19.416
meaning you and José Arcadio.

265
00:16:20.083 --> 00:16:22.250
the gringos can't even go near them.

266
00:16:25.208 --> 00:16:26.833
So if you still have those somewhere--

267
00:16:26.916 --> 00:16:29.541
I burned everything
when your brother died.

268
00:16:30.875 --> 00:16:32.666
All I kept of his…

269
00:16:35.791 --> 00:16:37.083
was this house.

270
00:16:38.625 --> 00:16:40.625
and this shotgun in my hands.

271
00:16:42.708 --> 00:16:43.541
[Aureliano] Hmm.

272
00:16:55.625 --> 00:16:57.583
It was nice to see you. Rebeca.

273
00:17:02.375 --> 00:17:03.250
Mm.

274
00:17:09.875 --> 00:17:11.875
[door hinge creaking]

275
00:17:11.958 --> 00:17:13.250
[door closes]

276
00:17:14.291 --> 00:17:16.208
[reverential music playing]

277
00:17:16.291 --> 00:17:20.083
[Fernanda in Latin]
"And renew the right spirit within me."

278
00:17:20.583 --> 00:17:22.916
"Do not cast me away from your face."

279
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.750
"And take not thy Holy Spirit from me."

280
00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:30.916
[in English] After having sinned.
David asks God to give him a pure heart.

281
00:17:31.958 --> 00:17:34.833
Because God always knows
when we have sinned.

282
00:17:35.791 --> 00:17:39.000
[in Latin] "Restore to me
the joy of your salvation."

283
00:17:40.208 --> 00:17:41.750
[knocking at door]

284
00:17:43.875 --> 00:17:46.125
"Strengthen me with your spirit."

285
00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.541
[music stops]

286
00:17:52.916 --> 00:17:54.666
[in English] The last guest just left.

287
00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.041
Can I go pee. Mom?

288
00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.166
Be careful. Meme.

289
00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:03.250
[footsteps rapidly thumping]

290
00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:08.125
Don't you want to rest for a bit.
José Arcadio?

291
00:18:09.416 --> 00:18:12.208
My son knows that he has to take
his education very seriously

292
00:18:12.291 --> 00:18:13.291
if he wants to go to Rome.

293
00:18:13.375 --> 00:18:16.000
But it is impossible to do so
when this house is full of sinful men

294
00:18:16.083 --> 00:18:18.541
day and night
who may lead him down the path of evil.

295
00:18:19.625 --> 00:18:23.000
It is a Christian value
to help those who are in need.

296
00:18:23.666 --> 00:18:25.083
It's in the Bible.

297
00:18:25.166 --> 00:18:26.958
They are vagabonds. Úrsula.

298
00:18:27.875 --> 00:18:31.250
They're taking advantage of you.
and you seem to like that.

299
00:18:31.833 --> 00:18:34.583
Don't forget
you are in my house. Fernanda.

300
00:18:35.125 --> 00:18:39.416
I opened my doors to those foreigners
with the same generosity as I did for you.

301
00:18:40.375 --> 00:18:41.708
And all of your saints.

302
00:18:44.875 --> 00:18:46.375
Come to think of it.

303
00:18:47.125 --> 00:18:49.208
today is October 4th…

304
00:18:51.208 --> 00:18:55.333
which just so happens to be the day
of the loved Saint Francis of Assisi.

305
00:18:57.083 --> 00:18:58.583
The saint of poverty…

306
00:19:02.375 --> 00:19:04.083
and humility.

307
00:19:24.333 --> 00:19:25.875
[dark ethereal music playing]

308
00:19:45.208 --> 00:19:46.791
[Aureliano] <i>She's alive. Mama.</i>

309
00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:50.875
<i>She's alive.</i>

310
00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:54.083
[Úrsula] <i>God forgive me.</i>

311
00:19:56.041 --> 00:19:57.500
[music fades]

312
00:19:57.583 --> 00:20:00.958
[sobs] What kind of mother
would neglect their child all these years?

313
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.166
Did you know she was alive?

314
00:20:14.083 --> 00:20:16.041
[young José Arcadio]
Auntie. I was looking for you.

315
00:20:16.666 --> 00:20:17.625
[Amaranta chuckles]

316
00:20:19.375 --> 00:20:23.208
[narrator] <i>The only one who never forgot.</i>
<i>even for a single minute.</i>

317
00:20:23.291 --> 00:20:26.916
<i>that Rebeca was alive.</i>
<i>rotting in a soup of maggots.</i>

318
00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:31.208
<i>was the ruthless and aging Amaranta.</i>

319
00:20:32.375 --> 00:20:34.333
<i>She thought of her at dawn.</i>

320
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.291
<i>and every time she changed.</i>

321
00:20:36.375 --> 00:20:40.166
<i>the black bandage of terrible atonement</i>
<i>wrapped around her hand.</i>

322
00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:41.958
[mysterious music playing]

323
00:20:44.625 --> 00:20:47.666
[Aureliano II] After saving
an entire village of people.

324
00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.791
all who hadn't slept for months.

325
00:20:49.875 --> 00:20:52.166
I decided to write that book.

326
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.125
[young Meme] What's it about?

327
00:20:54.208 --> 00:20:56.333
[Aureliano II] I cannot tell you.
beautiful Meme.

328
00:20:56.916 --> 00:20:59.208
No one must understand its meaning.

329
00:20:59.708 --> 00:21:03.375
not until 100 years have passed.

330
00:21:03.458 --> 00:21:05.583
[laughter]

331
00:21:07.166 --> 00:21:09.541
- [music stops]
- [Aureliano II clears throat]

332
00:21:13.125 --> 00:21:14.458
And why are you dressed like that?

333
00:21:15.208 --> 00:21:17.333
He's telling us the story of Melquiades.

334
00:21:18.458 --> 00:21:22.375
Can't say I'm surprised. Renata.
Sin has always come naturally to you.

335
00:21:22.458 --> 00:21:24.625
But you. José Arcadio.
I would have never expected you--

336
00:21:24.708 --> 00:21:27.291
I went and woke them up.
Don't reprimand them.

337
00:21:27.375 --> 00:21:30.375
For years. I allowed you
to humiliate and abandon us.

338
00:21:30.458 --> 00:21:32.250
Do you know where
your children are eating now?

339
00:21:32.333 --> 00:21:34.250
In their quarters. like a pair of dogs.

340
00:21:34.333 --> 00:21:37.791
Because. apparently. Úrsula's guests
are far more important than any of us are.

341
00:21:37.875 --> 00:21:39.958
Stop being so dramatic. Fernanda.

342
00:21:40.041 --> 00:21:41.750
[Fernanda] You do nothing for us.

343
00:21:42.250 --> 00:21:44.166
And meanwhile. you get it all.

344
00:21:44.666 --> 00:21:46.166
Even your little concubine.

345
00:21:46.250 --> 00:21:48.208
What is a concubine?

346
00:21:48.958 --> 00:21:52.083
It's the lady that we met
at the train station that day.

347
00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:58.458
[woman] You'll be begging for forgiveness!

348
00:21:59.416 --> 00:22:00.458
[narrator] <i>That same day.</i>

349
00:22:00.541 --> 00:22:04.583
<i>Fernanda sent Aureliano's trunk of clothes</i>
<i>to his concubine's house.</i>

350
00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:06.958
<i>She sent them in broad daylight.</i>

351
00:22:07.041 --> 00:22:09.500
<i>and ordered that they'd be carried</i>
<i>down the middle of the street</i>

352
00:22:09.583 --> 00:22:10.875
<i>for everyone to see…</i>

353
00:22:10.958 --> 00:22:11.916
[woman 2] How shameless.

354
00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:15.791
<i>…believing that her wayward husband</i>
<i>would be unable to bear the shame</i>

355
00:22:15.875 --> 00:22:18.458
<i>and would return home</i>
<i>with his head hung low.</i>

356
00:22:18.541 --> 00:22:20.541
[laughing]

357
00:22:21.208 --> 00:22:23.375
[woman 3] Shameful. Both of them.

358
00:22:24.166 --> 00:22:25.416
You're disgraceful!

359
00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:26.791
[woman 2] What a dog!

360
00:22:27.833 --> 00:22:29.166
[man 1] You have no shame.

361
00:22:30.041 --> 00:22:32.041
[people murmuring]

362
00:22:43.625 --> 00:22:45.625
[mysterious music playing]

363
00:22:46.541 --> 00:22:48.875
[overhead clattering]

364
00:22:57.291 --> 00:22:58.458
[man pants] Remedios.

365
00:22:59.208 --> 00:23:00.625
What are you doing up there?

366
00:23:01.541 --> 00:23:03.041
I don't know what's wrong with me.

367
00:23:04.416 --> 00:23:06.416
All I think about is seeing you.

368
00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:07.791
You should get down.

369
00:23:07.875 --> 00:23:09.291
The roof's not safe.

370
00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:15.083
Let me put soap on your back at least.

371
00:23:17.833 --> 00:23:20.041
I don't think anyone's ever put soap
on their back.

372
00:23:26.416 --> 00:23:27.666
[screams]

373
00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:29.000
[loud thud]

374
00:23:29.083 --> 00:23:31.083
[dark music playing]

375
00:23:36.208 --> 00:23:37.416
[Úrsula] Good heavens!

376
00:23:38.791 --> 00:23:39.958
Remedios.

377
00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.000
[train whistle blowing]

378
00:23:52.708 --> 00:23:53.750
[whistle blows]

379
00:23:53.833 --> 00:23:57.291
[Mr. Herbert] Oh. here he is.
Welcome to Macondo. Mr. Brown.

380
00:23:58.125 --> 00:24:00.583
- Mr. Herbert. how you doing?
- Great. great. great.

381
00:24:00.666 --> 00:24:01.916
This is the town's new mayor.

382
00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.458
At your service. Mr. Brown.

383
00:24:03.541 --> 00:24:04.625
- Nice to meet you. sir.
- Sir.

384
00:24:04.708 --> 00:24:06.916
Now. if you come this way. we'll. uh…

385
00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.958
Is it always this hot?
It's hotter than Hades.

386
00:24:09.041 --> 00:24:12.750
Oh. it certainly is.
but you do get used to it.

387
00:24:12.833 --> 00:24:14.250
- Okay. I hope so.
- And it's…

388
00:24:14.333 --> 00:24:16.333
Uh. the train is new to town. so…

389
00:24:16.416 --> 00:24:18.416
- It might feel…
- No. no. no. no. no.

390
00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:22.083
[narrator] <i>Mr. Jack Brown arrived</i>
<i>in Macondo on a hot Wednesday.</i>

391
00:24:22.166 --> 00:24:24.500
<i>straight from Prattville. Alabama.</i>

392
00:24:24.583 --> 00:24:27.833
<i>He was followed everywhere</i>
<i>by a pack of ferocious hounds.</i>

393
00:24:27.916 --> 00:24:31.041
<i>engineers. topographers.</i>
<i>and land surveyors.</i>

394
00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:34.083
<i>Nobody knew what they were looking for.</i>

395
00:24:34.750 --> 00:24:36.833
- Go ahead and set that down there.
- Sir. it's ready.

396
00:24:36.916 --> 00:24:38.375
Take my cane. Thank you.

397
00:24:38.458 --> 00:24:40.916
[narrator] <i>Endowed with resources</i>
<i>that in a different era</i>

398
00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:43.458
<i>would have been reserved</i>
<i>only for divine providence…</i>

399
00:24:43.541 --> 00:24:45.000
José Arcadio! My horse!

400
00:24:45.083 --> 00:24:47.750
<i>…the foreigners altered</i>
<i>the rainfall patterns.</i>

401
00:24:47.833 --> 00:24:50.666
<i>moved the river</i>
<i>from where it had always been.</i>

402
00:24:50.750 --> 00:24:53.208
<i>and put it on the other side of the town.</i>

403
00:25:01.291 --> 00:25:05.500
<i>And at the newly established</i>
<i>banana business. the United Fruit Company.</i>

404
00:25:05.583 --> 00:25:08.541
<i>José Arcadio Segundo</i>
<i>found work as a foreman.</i>

405
00:25:09.041 --> 00:25:11.375
[José Arcadio II] <i>Gentlemen! Welcome!</i>

406
00:25:12.041 --> 00:25:15.458
In the coming days. you will all discover
that the working conditions we offer

407
00:25:15.541 --> 00:25:17.666
are the best you'll find along the coast.

408
00:25:18.166 --> 00:25:20.500
Because our company
is the largest company there is

409
00:25:20.583 --> 00:25:22.208
in the whole area.

410
00:25:23.250 --> 00:25:24.958
We take care of the entire process.

411
00:25:25.041 --> 00:25:28.208
from the moment we cut the banana
to its exportation.

412
00:25:32.291 --> 00:25:34.375
[indistinct chattering]

413
00:25:34.458 --> 00:25:37.916
Part of your compensation
is issued in these vouchers.

414
00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:41.000
which are redeemable
at the town's local commissary

415
00:25:41.083 --> 00:25:43.291
for imported products such as these.

416
00:25:43.375 --> 00:25:45.875
You should all feel privileged

417
00:25:46.583 --> 00:25:49.916
because there is no place in Macondo
or in the entire country

418
00:25:50.000 --> 00:25:53.458
where you can get the best quality
ham products from Virginia.

419
00:25:55.166 --> 00:25:58.875
This here is our gift to you
for your loyal service.

420
00:25:58.958 --> 00:26:01.000
[cheering]

421
00:26:01.083 --> 00:26:03.083
[suspenseful music playing]

422
00:26:07.375 --> 00:26:09.375
- José Arcadio.
- Mr. Brown.

423
00:26:11.166 --> 00:26:12.666
[José Arcadio II] Please enjoy it.

424
00:26:13.333 --> 00:26:16.458
Explore the town and get some rest

425
00:26:16.541 --> 00:26:19.250
because tomorrow
we start bright and early at 6:00.

426
00:26:19.750 --> 00:26:22.875
So welcome to the United Fruit Family!

427
00:26:22.958 --> 00:26:26.541
[cheering]

428
00:26:26.625 --> 00:26:28.375
- [man] Looks good.
- [José Arcadio II] Welcome.

429
00:26:28.458 --> 00:26:30.416
Hey. go grab some ham. It's American.

430
00:26:30.916 --> 00:26:32.916
Welcome. Welcome.

431
00:26:42.458 --> 00:26:44.458
[ethereal music playing]

432
00:26:53.208 --> 00:26:56.166
[narrator] <i>Until her very last minute</i>
<i>on Earth.</i>

433
00:26:56.750 --> 00:26:59.500
<i>Remedios the Beauty remained unaware</i>

434
00:26:59.583 --> 00:27:03.208
<i>that her inescapable</i>
<i>and unsettling female nature</i>

435
00:27:03.291 --> 00:27:05.041
<i>was a daily disaster.</i>

436
00:27:08.041 --> 00:27:11.166
[indistinct chattering]

437
00:27:15.291 --> 00:27:18.875
[José Arcadio II] The bananas are
transported along these rails to the exit.

438
00:27:20.250 --> 00:27:24.041
From there. they're taken to the train
and from the train to the port.

439
00:27:24.666 --> 00:27:27.500
where the bananas are loaded
onto company ships.

440
00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:34.000
[ethereal music continues]

441
00:27:34.083 --> 00:27:36.416
[wind whistling]

442
00:28:05.166 --> 00:28:07.166
[rattling]

443
00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:16.708
[rattling stops]

444
00:28:16.791 --> 00:28:18.666
[music swells]

445
00:28:18.750 --> 00:28:20.750
[train whistle blowing]

446
00:28:45.833 --> 00:28:47.291
Hello. good afternoon.

447
00:28:49.125 --> 00:28:51.125
[unsettling ethereal music playing]

448
00:29:02.958 --> 00:29:04.958
[insects chittering]

449
00:29:08.666 --> 00:29:12.083
[narrator] <i>From the moment</i>
<i>Remedios stepped onto the plantation.</i>

450
00:29:12.166 --> 00:29:15.208
<i>the air was impregnated</i>
<i>with a deadly fragrance.</i>

451
00:29:15.916 --> 00:29:20.958
<i>The men working in the ditches</i>
<i>felt possessed by a strange fascination.</i>

452
00:29:22.125 --> 00:29:25.208
<i>threatened by an invisible danger.</i>

453
00:29:25.291 --> 00:29:28.625
<i>and many succumbing</i>
<i>to the terrible urge to weep.</i>

454
00:29:28.708 --> 00:29:30.500
- [man 1] Get back!
- [men grunting]

455
00:29:32.166 --> 00:29:33.083
[man 2] Let go!

456
00:29:34.208 --> 00:29:36.541
- [man 3] What do you think you're doing?
- [men scream]

457
00:29:43.666 --> 00:29:45.666
- [panting]
- [music fades]

458
00:29:51.791 --> 00:29:54.250
[José Arcadio II]
And that's extremely important to us

459
00:29:54.333 --> 00:29:57.791
because we have to deliver them
perfectly clean.

460
00:29:58.625 --> 00:29:59.833
What did you think of the tour?

461
00:29:59.916 --> 00:30:01.250
[Úrsula] I would've never imagined

462
00:30:01.333 --> 00:30:03.500
that you could have this many
in one place.

463
00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:06.750
Darling! What happened? What's wrong?

464
00:30:06.833 --> 00:30:08.708
Why don't you have your hat. Remedios?

465
00:30:08.791 --> 00:30:10.958
[Úrsula] Oh my God. Remedios.

466
00:30:16.666 --> 00:30:17.666
Come on. boys.

467
00:30:18.166 --> 00:30:20.500
[man] Let's go. let's go. let's go!
Grab your machetes!

468
00:30:23.708 --> 00:30:25.708
[tense percussive music playing]

469
00:30:34.125 --> 00:30:35.750
[music fades]

470
00:30:35.833 --> 00:30:38.708
[Mr. Brown] My best whiskey.
Directly from Canada.

471
00:30:45.833 --> 00:30:47.708
- Pretty smooth. huh?
- [laughs]

472
00:30:51.541 --> 00:30:53.458
Did your family enjoy the visit?

473
00:30:54.291 --> 00:30:55.291
[José Arcadio II] Mm.

474
00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:57.083
[in Spanish] That's good.

475
00:30:57.166 --> 00:30:58.541
[José Arcadio II in English] Yes.

476
00:30:58.625 --> 00:31:01.791
Except two of my men died
on the plantation today.

477
00:31:04.041 --> 00:31:05.416
An accident.

478
00:31:06.666 --> 00:31:08.458
Well. that's very sad to hear.

479
00:31:13.125 --> 00:31:14.958
Got any more news to share?

480
00:31:16.500 --> 00:31:18.166
More men keep coming.

481
00:31:22.041 --> 00:31:24.083
We're starting with two full crews
tomorrow morning.

482
00:31:25.333 --> 00:31:26.875
We'll need to expand the barracks.

483
00:31:26.958 --> 00:31:28.958
These boys are coming from far away.

484
00:31:30.166 --> 00:31:31.500
We'll take care of that.

485
00:31:36.041 --> 00:31:37.208
Anything else?

486
00:31:39.125 --> 00:31:40.333
Yes. Mr. Brown.

487
00:31:43.333 --> 00:31:45.250
We should build a health center here

488
00:31:45.750 --> 00:31:47.875
for emergencies.
like the one we had today.

489
00:31:50.666 --> 00:31:51.958
It's a good idea.

490
00:31:54.125 --> 00:31:55.750
I'll make sure they see to that.

491
00:32:00.333 --> 00:32:02.250
Oh. Buendía. Hang on a sec.

492
00:32:03.875 --> 00:32:04.958
Take these.

493
00:32:10.708 --> 00:32:13.083
Some nice coupons for the commissary.

494
00:32:15.791 --> 00:32:17.375
Good job. Buendía.

495
00:32:19.916 --> 00:32:22.250
Honey. could you come in here a second?

496
00:32:23.583 --> 00:32:24.666
[José Arcadio II] Mm.

497
00:32:26.541 --> 00:32:27.375
Sir?

498
00:32:28.875 --> 00:32:30.291
[young Meme] Does it hurt. Auntie?

499
00:32:33.375 --> 00:32:34.958
Why did they do that to you?

500
00:32:35.541 --> 00:32:39.250
[Aureliano] Because the people
in this town are going mad.

501
00:32:40.791 --> 00:32:42.125
[Fernanda] It's not just that.

502
00:32:42.833 --> 00:32:45.166
It's because Remedios is provocative.

503
00:32:45.708 --> 00:32:48.583
We've seen how she walks around naked
with no sense of modesty

504
00:32:48.666 --> 00:32:51.291
so that the men Great-Grandmother
invites over can gawk at her.

505
00:32:51.375 --> 00:32:54.750
[Aureliano] Hey! Show some respect.
you ungrateful city brat.

506
00:32:58.250 --> 00:33:00.375
Modesty is for people like you. Fernanda.

507
00:33:01.250 --> 00:33:04.583
who have to pray day and night
to drive the evil out of their souls.

508
00:33:10.708 --> 00:33:12.166
I'm just telling the truth.

509
00:33:12.666 --> 00:33:15.083
Your aunt isn't just crazy.
She's extremely dangerous.

510
00:33:15.166 --> 00:33:16.500
[knocking at door]

511
00:33:16.583 --> 00:33:17.541
[man] Mail!

512
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:22.000
[door opens]

513
00:33:23.083 --> 00:33:25.416
[young José Arcadio]
Presents from Grandpa. Come on. Meme!

514
00:33:26.916 --> 00:33:28.000
[man] We'll put it here.

515
00:33:29.125 --> 00:33:30.916
[young José Arcadio] Wait. Meme. Hold it.

516
00:33:33.708 --> 00:33:34.708
Whoa.

517
00:33:39.625 --> 00:33:41.333
I wanna see what it is.

518
00:33:45.791 --> 00:33:47.791
[young José Arcadio pants. sobs]

519
00:33:48.708 --> 00:33:50.166
[young Meme screams]

520
00:33:51.416 --> 00:33:53.416
[children crying]

521
00:33:55.416 --> 00:33:57.916
- [Fernanda crying]
- [somber music playing]

522
00:34:01.833 --> 00:34:03.375
[screams] No!

523
00:34:09.666 --> 00:34:11.958
[in Spanish] My dad! [sobs]

524
00:34:12.041 --> 00:34:14.041
[somber music continues]

525
00:34:26.041 --> 00:34:27.166
[music stops]

526
00:34:35.875 --> 00:34:37.875
[dramatic music playing]

527
00:34:58.875 --> 00:35:00.875
[music turns lively]

528
00:35:26.666 --> 00:35:27.958
[in English] Get out!

529
00:35:28.041 --> 00:35:29.291
[music stops]

530
00:35:33.541 --> 00:35:38.000
How could you tarnish my father's memory
in such a horrible way?

531
00:35:40.875 --> 00:35:43.333
A Christian man has died. Aureliano.

532
00:35:44.166 --> 00:35:45.750
A man. not a dog!

533
00:35:46.250 --> 00:35:48.250
[murmuring]

534
00:35:51.333 --> 00:35:53.125
This is our homage to your father.

535
00:35:55.083 --> 00:35:56.958
Ma. I didn't do anything.

536
00:35:57.041 --> 00:35:58.791
It was Meme and Papa.

537
00:35:58.875 --> 00:36:00.083
Shut up. you snitch.

538
00:36:00.166 --> 00:36:01.708
[Úrsula] Fernanda. it wasn't just him.

539
00:36:01.791 --> 00:36:03.875
- It was also my idea--
- Stay out of it. please. Úrsula.

540
00:36:04.375 --> 00:36:05.916
It's not your concern.

541
00:36:09.125 --> 00:36:11.791
I accepted this failed marriage for you

542
00:36:11.875 --> 00:36:14.041
and everyone's gross incivility

543
00:36:14.125 --> 00:36:17.375
so I could raise my children
in a Christian household.

544
00:36:17.916 --> 00:36:20.791
But I've come to realize
that. time and time again.

545
00:36:21.375 --> 00:36:23.875
in this insane house. it's impossible.

546
00:36:27.750 --> 00:36:29.458
The children are leaving Macondo!

547
00:36:30.791 --> 00:36:32.333
You can't take my children.

548
00:36:34.916 --> 00:36:35.833
I can

549
00:36:37.041 --> 00:36:38.750
because I am their mama.

550
00:36:38.833 --> 00:36:40.458
And it's them I chose.

551
00:36:42.083 --> 00:36:44.666
But not you. You chose her instead.

552
00:36:49.666 --> 00:36:51.791
[melancholy music playing]

553
00:36:51.875 --> 00:36:54.916
[Úrsula] For God's sake. Fernanda.
How can you say that?

554
00:36:55.625 --> 00:36:57.666
I packed you all of your favorite treats.

555
00:36:58.458 --> 00:37:01.125
But you shouldn't eat them
all at once. all right?

556
00:37:01.208 --> 00:37:02.333
You promise me?

557
00:37:04.833 --> 00:37:07.708
Well. come here. Let's get you changed.

558
00:37:07.791 --> 00:37:09.083
- Come on.
- [sobs]

559
00:37:16.791 --> 00:37:18.791
[Úrsula sobs]

560
00:37:20.291 --> 00:37:22.208
It's beautiful.

561
00:37:22.291 --> 00:37:23.791
Thank you so much.

562
00:37:29.875 --> 00:37:32.833
[young Meme] Auntie.
aren't you coming to the station?

563
00:37:38.833 --> 00:37:40.375
I love you very much.

564
00:37:41.125 --> 00:37:42.375
Have fun. okay?

565
00:37:46.541 --> 00:37:48.208
[young José Arcadio]
I'm going to miss you.

566
00:37:48.833 --> 00:37:49.916
Me too.

567
00:37:51.083 --> 00:37:53.541
José Arcadio. Let's go. sweetheart.

568
00:37:53.625 --> 00:37:55.625
[reverential music playing]

569
00:38:02.791 --> 00:38:05.916
Auntie. are you feeling all right?

570
00:38:07.625 --> 00:38:09.125
I've never felt better.

571
00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:12.750
[reverential music continues]

572
00:38:14.250 --> 00:38:16.041
I went through this myself. you know.

573
00:38:17.166 --> 00:38:19.250
But you and I came from royalty. Renata.

574
00:38:20.541 --> 00:38:22.916
- All queens are educated by nuns.
- [whistle blows]

575
00:38:24.791 --> 00:38:25.958
It's what's best for you.

576
00:38:26.041 --> 00:38:27.541
[train whistle blows]

577
00:38:33.625 --> 00:38:35.458
[whistle blows]

578
00:38:37.916 --> 00:38:40.208
- I'm gonna miss you. my love.
- Me too. Daddy.

579
00:38:40.291 --> 00:38:42.291
- Be a good girl.
- Okay.

580
00:38:44.708 --> 00:38:46.708
[sobs]

581
00:38:54.916 --> 00:38:56.041
Go with Grandma.

582
00:38:56.125 --> 00:38:58.000
- [whistle blows]
- [Úrsula] Oh. Meme.

583
00:38:58.083 --> 00:39:00.083
[bell rings]

584
00:39:01.333 --> 00:39:03.333
[melancholy music playing]

585
00:39:07.166 --> 00:39:08.000
[sniffles]

586
00:39:21.875 --> 00:39:23.916
[Úrsula] May God be with you. my children.

587
00:39:29.541 --> 00:39:31.458
Be a good girl. you hear me. Meme?

588
00:39:31.958 --> 00:39:33.125
Write me a letter every month.

589
00:39:33.208 --> 00:39:35.625
Daddy will be right here.
reading your letters.

590
00:39:37.041 --> 00:39:38.541
Don't ever forget that Daddy loves you.

591
00:39:38.625 --> 00:39:41.125
and that I'll be right here
waiting for you to come back!

592
00:39:45.458 --> 00:39:47.458
[steam hissing]

593
00:40:02.875 --> 00:40:04.166
[music fades]

594
00:40:04.250 --> 00:40:07.208
NEW RAILWAYS
WILL BOOST DEVELOPMENT IN MACONDO

595
00:40:07.291 --> 00:40:09.791
[Aureliano] My family
has lost their minds.

596
00:40:14.291 --> 00:40:17.416
Now it turns out
Macondo is going to have a pope

597
00:40:18.625 --> 00:40:19.958
and a saint.

598
00:40:21.833 --> 00:40:22.666
Mm.

599
00:40:23.333 --> 00:40:24.583
And a martyr.

600
00:40:25.083 --> 00:40:26.000
[Aureliano] Hmm.

601
00:40:27.125 --> 00:40:28.958
[Gerineldo] Haven't you seen it yet?

602
00:40:29.041 --> 00:40:30.083
[Aureliano] Hmm.

603
00:40:30.166 --> 00:40:32.166
[dark melancholy music playing]

604
00:40:33.083 --> 00:40:34.166
Mm-mm.

605
00:40:36.458 --> 00:40:40.791
IN MEMORY OF COLONEL AURELIANO BUENDÍA

606
00:40:40.875 --> 00:40:43.416
TIRELESS DEFENDER OF FREEDOM AND JUSTICE

607
00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:46.250
HIS FIGHT FOR A SOVEREIGN NATION
ENDURES IN THE HEARTS OF HIS PEOPLE

608
00:40:46.333 --> 00:40:48.583
[Aureliano] I guess
since they couldn't kill me…

609
00:40:50.958 --> 00:40:53.416
they wanna bury me alive. Gerineldo.

610
00:40:55.583 --> 00:40:56.500
[Aureliano] Mm.

611
00:41:05.708 --> 00:41:07.708
[indistinct chattering]

612
00:41:11.791 --> 00:41:13.208
[car horn honks]

613
00:41:16.125 --> 00:41:17.250
[car horn honks]

614
00:41:17.875 --> 00:41:19.458
[Aureliano] What's the matter with you?

615
00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:22.083
What's the hurry?

616
00:41:34.583 --> 00:41:39.250
Gerineldo. look at the mess
we've gotten ourselves into.

617
00:41:40.458 --> 00:41:44.750
All because we invited those fucking
banana-eating gringos into our town.

618
00:41:46.166 --> 00:41:49.000
- [jazz music playing]
- [car horn honks]

619
00:41:49.083 --> 00:41:51.083
[indistinct chattering]

620
00:41:53.416 --> 00:41:55.291
- Here you go.
- [officer] You work here. old man?

621
00:41:55.375 --> 00:41:57.708
[man] My son-in-law does.
The father of my grandson.

622
00:41:57.791 --> 00:41:59.666
[officer] You can't come in
unless you work here.

623
00:41:59.750 --> 00:42:01.291
This is for company workers only.

624
00:42:01.375 --> 00:42:04.625
But I have a voucher.
and the man who gave it to me works here.

625
00:42:05.125 --> 00:42:07.208
- Show me the voucher.
- You cannot forbid me to come in.

626
00:42:07.291 --> 00:42:09.833
- Show me the voucher. old man.
- Here's the voucher.

627
00:42:11.958 --> 00:42:13.916
You shouldn't have this. This is illegal.

628
00:42:14.000 --> 00:42:16.708
What you are doing is illegal.
You're nobody here.

629
00:42:16.791 --> 00:42:18.250
You don't have any authority.

630
00:42:18.333 --> 00:42:20.416
Put that back!
Hey. he's trying to steal this!

631
00:42:20.500 --> 00:42:22.625
- Manuel! Hey. don't touch him!
- Come here!

632
00:42:22.708 --> 00:42:24.000
[old man] Leave him alone!

633
00:42:24.083 --> 00:42:26.000
- Leave him alone! Manuel!
- [Manuel] Grandpa. help!

634
00:42:26.083 --> 00:42:27.791
[officer] Don't move! Shut up!

635
00:42:28.500 --> 00:42:29.916
[old man] Manuel!

636
00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.125
What have you done?

637
00:42:31.208 --> 00:42:33.208
- [blows land]
- [old man grunts]

638
00:42:38.541 --> 00:42:39.583
[blow lands]

639
00:42:40.208 --> 00:42:41.666
[Aureliano] Scum!

640
00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:43.666
Murderers!

641
00:42:45.083 --> 00:42:46.875
You bastards!

642
00:43:00.125 --> 00:43:01.125
Come on.

643
00:43:08.166 --> 00:43:10.666
[unsettling music playing]

644
00:43:10.750 --> 00:43:12.416
What's the matter with them?

645
00:43:13.416 --> 00:43:15.416
[people murmuring]

646
00:43:16.041 --> 00:43:17.166
What have we done?

647
00:43:17.250 --> 00:43:18.375
Come on. let's go.

648
00:43:21.291 --> 00:43:22.583
Please. Aureliano.

649
00:43:24.083 --> 00:43:25.958
What's happening. Gerineldo?

650
00:43:27.458 --> 00:43:29.458
[dark ethereal music playing]

651
00:43:42.416 --> 00:43:43.625
[officer] Hey. sir!

652
00:43:43.708 --> 00:43:45.416
Hey. where are you going? Sir!

653
00:43:46.125 --> 00:43:46.958
Hey!

654
00:43:47.666 --> 00:43:49.583
[music fades]

655
00:43:49.666 --> 00:43:51.166
What are you doing here. Colonel?

656
00:43:52.000 --> 00:43:54.250
I'm gonna tell that guy Mr. Brown

657
00:43:54.875 --> 00:43:57.583
that a murder was committed
by his own company.

658
00:43:58.083 --> 00:43:59.208
By United Fruit Co.?

659
00:43:59.291 --> 00:44:01.583
I suggest you get out of my way
if you don't want trouble.

660
00:44:01.666 --> 00:44:03.041
[guard] Everything all right?

661
00:44:05.833 --> 00:44:07.291
[José Arcadio II] Everything's fine.

662
00:44:11.750 --> 00:44:15.333
- The Conservative government…
- As I was saying. Mr. Brown…

663
00:44:16.333 --> 00:44:17.833
Huh? What's going on?

664
00:44:17.916 --> 00:44:19.250
[Aureliano] And what's worse.

665
00:44:19.750 --> 00:44:23.166
they gave you free rein
to do whatever you want!

666
00:44:24.750 --> 00:44:27.875
But know that here in Macondo.
there are still men

667
00:44:27.958 --> 00:44:30.250
that will never kneel to anyone

668
00:44:31.708 --> 00:44:34.458
and that are willing and ready to revolt.

669
00:44:35.583 --> 00:44:39.208
This time. against you
and your murderous organization.

670
00:44:42.958 --> 00:44:44.291
[Aureliano groans]

671
00:44:57.541 --> 00:45:00.083
[Aureliano scoffs] You bastards.

672
00:45:03.500 --> 00:45:05.625
- The hell's going on?
- Don't worry. Everything's fine.

673
00:45:05.708 --> 00:45:06.833
[guard] What did he want?

674
00:45:06.916 --> 00:45:08.916
[dark piano music playing]

675
00:45:09.958 --> 00:45:12.625
[people murmuring]

676
00:45:20.125 --> 00:45:22.125
[music intensifies]

677
00:47:03.833 --> 00:47:07.333
[narrator] <i>Úrsula was the only one</i>
<i>with enough serenity to understand</i>

678
00:47:07.416 --> 00:47:10.083
<i>the nature of that irreparable wind.</i>

679
00:47:10.958 --> 00:47:13.666
<i>She watched Remedios the Beauty.</i>

680
00:47:14.541 --> 00:47:18.125
<i>amid the dazzling flutter of the sheets</i>
<i>rising with her.</i>

681
00:47:19.041 --> 00:47:20.625
<i>passing through the sky</i>

682
00:47:20.708 --> 00:47:23.208
<i>where the four o'clock light</i>
<i>came to an end.</i>

683
00:47:24.500 --> 00:47:27.541
<i>as she disappeared forever</i>
<i>into the atmosphere.</i>

684
00:47:28.750 --> 00:47:32.333
<i>where not even the highest birds of memory</i>
<i>could reach her.</i>

685
00:47:40.875 --> 00:47:42.541
[music fades]

686
00:47:48.333 --> 00:47:50.333
[soft melodic music playing]

687
00:48:50.833 --> 00:48:52.125
[music fades]

688
00:48:52.208 --> 00:48:54.208
[dark percussive music playing]

689
00:49:43.375 --> 00:49:45.375
[music fades]

690
00:49:49.166 --> 00:49:51.166
[percussive ethereal music playing]

691
00:51:15.958 --> 00:51:17.416
[music fades]

692
00:51:17.500 --> 00:51:19.500
[dark percussive music playing]

693
00:52:21.375 --> 00:52:23.000
[music fades]

694
00:52:24.125 --> 00:52:26.125
[ethereal melancholy music playing]

695
00:56:11.541 --> 00:56:13.541
[music fades]
